# After the Zenodo release, add the concept DOI (it resolves to the latest version):
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
abstract: >-
  ARCOPY is an OpenSeesPy framework for the seismic assessment and cost-based
  retrofit optimization of existing two-dimensional reinforced concrete frames.
  It builds the frame model interactively, runs static, modal, EC8 response
  spectrum and linear time-history analyses, checks members to EN 1992-1-1 and
  EN 1998-3, and searches complete retrofit strategies (new RC shear walls plus
  iterative concrete jacketing) for the minimum total cost. The shear-wall
  layout can be searched by drift screening or by Bayesian optimization
  (Tree-structured Parzen Estimator, Optuna). Results are written to CSV/Excel
  files and to a Word retrofit report.
keywords:
  - OpenSeesPy
  - seismic assessment
  - seismic retrofit
  - reinforced concrete frames
  - Eurocode 8
  - shear walls
  - concrete jacketing
  - cost optimization
  - Bayesian optimization
